who reign on the
 mountain of death?

269
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:02,630
-Yes.

270
00:10:02,630 --> 00:10:03,760
If he were to lead
 us, your people

271
00:10:03,760 --> 00:10:05,010
could succeed in annihilating--

272
00:10:05,010 --> 00:10:06,430
-Silence, you old fool.

273
00:10:06,430 --> 00:10:08,040
You'll only destroy yourself.

274
00:10:08,040 --> 00:10:08,760
[GOBBLE-GOBBLE]

275
00:10:08,760 --> 00:10:11,250
-Samara, my queen,
 I beseech you.

276
00:10:11,250 --> 00:10:11,930
-I explore you.

277
00:10:11,930 --> 00:10:13,510
-He is the only hope we have.

278
00:10:13,510 --> 00:10:14,330
So don't take it away.

279
00:10:14,330 --> 00:10:15,450
-I command you to stop.

280
00:10:15,450 --> 00:10:16,730
-Send for this man.

281
00:10:16,730 --> 00:10:18,160
He lives in Charen.

282
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:19,510
Send for him before
 it's too late.

283
00:10:19,510 --> 00:10:20,900
-OK, what's his number?

284
00:10:20,900 --> 00:10:22,620
-Your people are tired.

285
00:10:22,620 --> 00:10:24,250
-You dare to make threats.

286
00:10:24,250 --> 00:10:25,990
-Uh-oh.

287
00:10:25,990 --> 00:10:28,750
-Get out or for you
 it'll be too late.

288
00:10:28,750 --> 00:10:30,620
-He's a chest of drawers.

289
00:10:30,620 --> 00:10:33,010
-OK.

290
00:10:33,010 --> 00:10:34,750
-Is that my puddle?

291
00:10:34,750 --> 00:10:36,250
-Oh.

292
00:10:36,250 --> 00:10:37,460
-Fine, jerk-face.

293
00:10:37,460 --> 00:10:38,560
-What was that?

294
00:10:38,560 --> 00:10:41,360
-Nothing.

295
00:10:41,360 --> 00:10:43,950
-OK, you're shapely.

296
00:10:43,950 --> 00:10:45,670
-Hi, I'm a chocolate bar.

297
00:10:45,670 --> 00:10:47,950
Break off bits of me
 and enjoy me all day.

298
00:10:51,330 --> 00:10:52,960
-Wow, she looks
 like she was carved

299
00:10:52,960 --> 00:10:54,390
to go on the bow of a ship.

300
00:10:54,390 --> 00:10:55,190
-Gladio has lied to you.

301
00:10:55,190 --> 00:10:57,230
The man from Charen
 is about to arrive.

302
00:10:57,230 --> 00:10:59,820
They must be meeting secretly.

303
00:10:59,820 --> 00:11:00,390
-What's his name?

304
00:11:00,390 --> 00:11:02,270
-Hercules.

305
00:11:02,270 --> 00:11:03,430
-Yup, that's my cue.

306
00:11:03,430 --> 00:11:04,360
Big Alan Steel.

307
00:11:04,360 --> 00:11:05,890
Splash me on in the morning.

308
00:11:05,890 --> 00:11:08,740
Wear the great smell
 of me all day long.

309
00:11:08,740 --> 00:11:11,000
-He's riding on
 the horse's neck.

310
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:11,970
That's gotta hurt.

311
00:11:11,970 --> 00:11:15,360
-(SINGING) I'll be coming
 round the mountain when I come.

312
00:11:15,360 --> 00:11:18,750
[MUMBLING]

313
00:11:18,750 --> 00:11:20,350
-Huh, it's a living.

314
00:11:20,350 --> 00:11:23,140
Huh.

315
00:11:23,140 --> 00:11:24,930
-His body makes me feel funny.

316
00:11:24,930 --> 00:11:27,200
-I know, I know.

317
00:11:27,200 --> 00:11:31,900
-In the big country,
 dreams stay with you.

318
00:11:31,900 --> 00:11:33,400
-Now this next part's
 here's a little tricky.

319
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:35,080
Gotta go between
 some trees here.

320
00:11:40,300 --> 00:11:43,170
-Hey, He took the
 good tablecloth.

321
00:11:43,170 --> 00:11:46,260
-(SINGING) Oh, who's the guy and
 he's got big pecs and they call

322
00:11:46,260 --> 00:11:47,720
him Herc-- Ho!

323
00:11:53,960 --> 00:11:54,460
-What?

324
00:11:54,460 --> 00:11:55,750
I musta missed the exit.

325
00:11:55,750 --> 00:11:56,450
Huh?
 What?

326
00:11:56,450 --> 00:11:56,950
No?

327
00:11:56,950 --> 00:11:58,540
I don't see the highway.

328
00:11:58,540 --> 00:12:01,770
-(IN UNISON) Hercu-lee,
 Hercu-laa, Hercu-lee,

329
00:12:01,770 --> 00:12:05,590
Hercu-laa-ha-ha-ha,
 Hercu-lee, Hercu-laa,

330
00:12:05,590 --> 00:12:09,080
my backpack's filled
 with pecs. [LAUGHTER]

331
00:12:09,080 --> 00:12:10,500
-You know the best
 scenic overlooks

332
00:12:10,500 --> 00:12:12,040
are the scenic
 overlooks that aren't

333
00:12:12,040 --> 00:12:13,440
marked as scenic overlooks.

334
00:12:13,440 --> 00:12:15,590
-It's true.

335
00:12:15,590 --> 00:12:17,460
-You know, it all starts
 looking the same after a while.

336
00:12:17,460 --> 00:12:19,950
-Pretty much.

337
00:12:19,950 --> 00:12:21,460
-I hate Mondays.

338
00:12:21,460 --> 00:12:21,960
Hah.

339
00:12:24,490 --> 00:12:25,130
-Ohh, sorry, Herc.

340
00:12:25,130 --> 00:12:27,620
I tripped.

341
00:12:27,620 --> 00:12:28,420
-I meant to do that.

342
00:12:28,420 --> 00:12:28,920
Hah.

343
00:12:31,690 --> 00:12:33,370
-Hey, he's got his
 thong on upside-down.

344
00:12:33,370 --> 00:12:34,270
-No, no.

345
00:12:37,910 --> 00:12:41,440
-Not the twins.

346
00:12:41,440 --> 00:12:42,270
-Oh, Rob Reiner, no.

347
00:12:45,190 --> 00:12:48,600
-There he goes.

348
00:12:48,600 --> 00:12:50,310
-It's a scrum.

349
00:12:50,310 --> 00:12:53,130
-Oh, he's wearing
 his swim trunks, eh?

350
00:12:53,130 --> 00:12:54,310
-Seize him

351
00:12:54,310 --> 00:12:55,150
-Father Murphy, no.

352
00:12:58,400 --> 00:13:00,880
-When you agree to
 a Greek all the way

353
00:13:00,880 --> 00:13:03,760
from your last cigarette.

354
00:13:03,760 --> 00:13:06,540
-Gymkata.

355
00:13:06,540 --> 00:13:07,300
-Ha ha.

356
00:13:07,300 --> 00:13:09,050
Meet semi-spear
 in his orchestra.

357
00:13:09,050 --> 00:13:11,380
Hahaha.

358
00:13:11,380 --> 00:13:13,790
-I enjoy being a guy.

359
00:13:13,790 --> 00:13:14,290
Yeah!

360
00:13:17,520 --> 00:13:18,760
-Clean-up on aisle five.

361
00:13:18,760 --> 00:13:19,260
Ha ha.

362
00:13:19,260 --> 00:13:21,310
I love that one.

363
00:13:21,310 --> 00:13:24,750
-Well, time for my Snickers.

364
00:13:24,750 --> 00:13:26,660
[NEIGH] What took you so long?

365
00:13:26,660 --> 00:13:29,660
I'm only kidding, Herc.

366
00:13:29,660 --> 00:13:33,340
-It's not nice to
 fool Mother Nature.

367
00:13:33,340 --> 00:13:35,300
Hm.

368
00:13:35,300 --> 00:13:35,930
Oh no.

369
00:13:35,930 --> 00:13:37,150
The smoke alarm again.

370
00:13:37,150 --> 00:13:40,820
Every time I heat a glazed
 donut in the microwave--

371
00:13:40,820 --> 00:13:42,700
-Huh?

372
00:13:42,700 --> 00:13:43,200
Oh.

373
00:13:43,200 --> 00:13:44,390
-It's Hamlet's dad.

374
00:13:44,390 --> 00:13:45,320
Wrong film.

375
00:13:48,110 --> 00:13:51,630
-Oh, that's right it's Thursday.

376
00:13:51,630 --> 00:13:53,930
-It's a vision of
 a Mexican wrestler.

377
00:13:53,930 --> 00:13:57,320
-El Santo, I'm glad you're here.

378
00:13:57,320 --> 00:13:59,330
-The ghost of Christmas Cuckoo.

379
00:13:59,330 --> 00:14:01,260
-Samara, you have failed.

380
00:14:01,260 --> 00:14:02,520
Hercules is alive.

381
00:14:02,520 --> 00:14:05,120
He escaped from the
 trap you set for him.

382
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:06,330
-He chewed his leg off.

383
00:14:06,330 --> 00:14:07,140
-Alive?

384
00:14:07,140 --> 00:14:10,680
But how could he avoid death at
 the hands of my best soldiers?

385
00:14:10,680 --> 00:14:13,070
-You underestimated that man.

386
00:14:13,070 --> 00:14:15,910
-As long as he stays
 alive he remains a threat

387
00:14:15,910 --> 00:14:18,140
to that destiny
 written in the stars.

388
00:14:18,140 --> 00:14:20,130
We will not be able
 to leave the mountain.

389
00:14:20,130 --> 00:14:21,640
-We will not be undersold.

390
00:14:21,640 --> 00:14:24,800
-And you will not become the
 most powerful woman on earth.

391
00:14:24,800 --> 00:14:25,350
-I promise you.

392
00:14:25,350 --> 00:14:26,390
He will die.

393
00:14:26,390 --> 00:14:31,750
[THEME MUSIC]

394
00:14:31,750 --> 00:14:33,020
-Billis.

395
00:14:33,020 --> 00:14:33,980
-My love.

396
00:14:33,980 --> 00:14:34,480
-Say--

397
00:14:38,030 --> 00:14:39,470
-Hey, who told him
 that was a good look?

398
00:14:39,470 --> 00:14:41,340
-When are we going to meet
 openly in front of everyone?

399
00:14:41,340 --> 00:14:43,120
I'm going to speak
 to your sister.

400
00:14:43,120 --> 00:14:44,350
-Not in that, you're not.

401
00:14:44,350 --> 00:14:45,090
-No, don't go.

402
00:14:45,090 --> 00:14:46,500
-Why are you so frightened?

403
00:14:46,500 --> 00:14:50,100
After your own, my family
 is the most noble on Samar.

404
00:14:50,100 --> 00:14:51,280
-I've tried many times.

405
00:14:51,280 --> 00:14:52,850
-Oh, cross your legs, please.

406
00:14:52,850 --> 00:14:55,780
-To speak to her of my
 future and of our love.

407
00:14:55,780 --> 00:14:58,490
But I've always found
 Samara strangely hostile.

408
00:14:58,490 --> 00:14:59,310
-Yeah, but what a bod.

409
00:14:59,310 --> 00:15:01,290
-Your sister brings only
 sadness to everyone.

410
00:15:01,290 --> 00:15:02,140
That's not fair to her.

411
00:15:02,140 --> 00:15:03,270
-Face the facts.

412
00:15:03,270 --> 00:15:04,630
The people are suffering.

413
00:15:04,630 --> 00:15:06,150
They want to free
 themselves from fear.

414
00:15:06,150 --> 00:15:08,040
They want to destroy the
 monsters of the mouth, mountain

415
00:15:08,040 --> 00:15:09,520
and now they might
 be able to do it.

416
00:15:09,520 --> 00:15:10,190
-Is he a drum major?

417
00:15:10,190 --> 00:15:10,990
-We could wipe them out.

418
00:15:10,990 --> 00:15:13,910
But the queen is
 still opposed to it.

419
00:15:13,910 --> 00:15:16,040
-To fight against the mysterious
 power of the monsters--

420
00:15:16,040 --> 00:15:18,170
No one has ever
 dared to do that.

421
00:15:18,170 --> 00:15:19,160
I'm frightened Darix.

422
00:15:19,160 --> 00:15:19,660
-Don't worry.

423
00:15:19,660 --> 00:15:21,970
-I'm frightened, Darix, two too.

424
00:15:21,970 --> 00:15:23,630
-I don't intend to lose you.

425
00:15:23,630 --> 00:15:26,150
I love you and I
 intend to marry you.

426
00:15:26,150 --> 00:15:27,330
As soon as possible.

427
00:15:27,330 --> 00:15:28,850
-After I finish school.

428
00:15:28,850 --> 00:15:30,450
-I'll speak to Samara.

429
00:15:30,450 --> 00:15:31,030
[COUGHING]

430
00:15:31,030 --> 00:15:32,350
-She'll hear me out to the end.

431
00:15:32,350 --> 00:15:32,850
I swear it.

432
00:15:32,850 --> 00:15:34,720
-And if she doesn't
 give her consent?

433
00:15:34,720 --> 00:15:35,330
-Oh, Darix.

434
00:15:35,330 --> 00:15:36,580
-This is my little
 friend, Gorgon.

435
00:15:36,580 --> 00:15:38,410
Say hello to the folks, Gorgon.

436
00:15:38,410 --> 00:15:39,160
-Hello, folks.

437
00:15:39,160 --> 00:15:40,290
-Ow-ow-ow-ow-ow-ow-ow-ow-ow-ow-ow.

438
00:15:45,010 --> 00:15:45,960
-Are you Hercules?

439
00:15:45,960 --> 00:15:47,000
-I could be.

440
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:48,340
-Yes, who are you?

441
00:15:48,340 --> 00:15:48,920
What do you want?

442
00:15:48,920 --> 00:15:50,870
-I'm to lead you to the
 man who sent for you.

443
00:15:50,870 --> 00:15:51,410
-She's a smurf.

444
00:15:51,410 --> 00:15:53,710
-All right, up with you.

445
00:15:53,710 --> 00:15:56,660
-I think I'm sitting
 on the saddle horn.

446
00:15:56,660 --> 00:15:58,970
-As a boy, you weren't
 very convincing.

447
00:15:58,970 --> 00:16:01,460
-I'm Agar, daughter of Gladio.

448
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:03,110
-What makes your father
 send a girl to meet me.

449
00:16:03,110 --> 00:16:04,200
And a child at that.

450
00:16:04,200 --> 00:16:07,240
-I've no brothers and
 my father trusts in me.

451
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:08,290
-Stop talking so fast.

452
00:16:08,290 --> 00:16:09,520
-For the cause of
 liberty and justice

453
00:16:09,520 --> 00:16:11,140
I'm ready to do anything.

454
00:16:11,140 --> 00:16:12,560
-Even to fight?

455
00:16:12,560 --> 00:16:13,060
-That too.

456
00:16:13,060 --> 00:16:14,480
If it's necessary.

457
00:16:14,480 --> 00:16:15,350
-Would you fight me?

458
00:16:15,350 --> 00:16:16,010
-Let's go.

459
00:16:16,010 --> 00:16:19,020
I'll take you into Samar by
 a route that only I know.

460
00:16:19,020 --> 00:16:22,200
-By the way, do you ever bathe?

461
00:16:22,200 --> 00:16:23,330
-Ow-ow-ow-ow-ow-ow-ow-ow-ow-ow-ow.

462
00:16:30,540 --> 00:16:31,040
-Pizza, pizza.

463
00:16:35,050 --> 00:16:36,400
-It is bassoon.

464
00:16:40,960 --> 00:16:42,990
-Hey, this is my nice.

465
00:16:42,990 --> 00:16:43,820
-It's the queen.

466
00:16:43,820 --> 00:16:44,820
We must hide.

467
00:16:44,820 --> 00:16:48,360
-Duhhh-- OK.

468
00:16:48,360 --> 00:16:49,600
-This is wild.

469
00:16:49,600 --> 00:16:50,900
I swear.

470
00:16:50,900 --> 00:16:56,090
[CHUCKLING] Hey, how long
 do I have to hide back here?

471
00:16:56,090 --> 00:16:56,920
Oo--
 -Shh.

472
00:16:56,920 --> 00:16:57,420
Shut up.

473
00:16:57,420 --> 00:16:59,780
-I saw you leaving the
 city at daybreak, Agar.

474
00:16:59,780 --> 00:17:01,260
-I'm greatly honored
 that my queen should

475
00:17:01,260 --> 00:17:03,030
take the trouble
 to watch over me.

476
00:17:03,030 --> 00:17:04,870
-If I do so it's
 for your own good.

477
00:17:04,870 --> 00:17:08,470
[GROWLING]

478
00:17:08,470 --> 00:17:09,590
-And you were young.

479
00:17:09,590 --> 00:17:11,680
So young.

480
00:17:11,680 --> 00:17:12,830
You should be more prudent.

481
00:17:12,830 --> 00:17:15,370
[SNIFFING] Wow, smells
 like Gold's Gym in here.

482
00:17:15,370 --> 00:17:16,600
-Witch rhymes with--

483
00:17:16,600 --> 00:17:17,690
-What was that?

484
00:17:17,690 --> 00:17:18,780
-Nothing, nothing, nothing.

485
00:17:23,690 --> 00:17:25,830
-Look, It's a Mike
 Douglas show set.

486
00:17:25,830 --> 00:17:26,670
-Hercules, she's gone.

487
00:17:26,670 --> 00:17:27,370
You can come out now.

488
00:17:27,370 --> 00:17:27,870
-I knew that.

489
00:17:32,690 --> 00:17:36,060
-I'm writing a spec
 script for Aristophanes.

490
00:17:36,060 --> 00:17:38,880
-Let me thank you, Hercules--
 For answering my prayer.

491
00:17:38,880 --> 00:17:41,550
-It was my father's friendship
 for you that brought me here.

492
00:17:41,550 --> 00:17:43,540
-Did anyone see you?

493
00:17:43,540 --> 00:17:44,870
-Gotta go, gotta go,
 gotta go, gotta go.

494
00:17:44,870 --> 00:17:45,470
Sorry.
 Bye.

495
00:17:45,470 --> 00:17:48,600
-But a few weeks in Samar, I was
 ambushed by a band of ruffians.

496
00:17:48,600 --> 00:17:50,240
They must have mistaken
 me for a rich merchant

497
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:51,570
with sacks of gold.

498
00:17:51,570 --> 00:17:53,270
I changed their minds for them.

499
00:17:53,270 --> 00:17:54,110
-Bandits.

500
00:17:54,110 --> 00:17:55,230
-Hajji, Johnny, Race.

501
00:17:55,230 --> 00:17:56,320
-That's strange.

502
00:17:56,320 --> 00:18:00,600
All the roads that lead to Samar
 are always carefully guarded.

503
00:18:00,600 --> 00:18:03,070
Did you get a chance to
 see who their leader was?

504
00:18:03,070 --> 00:18:04,040
-Was it a guy with a big hat?

505
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:05,280
-He had a thick
 black beard and there

506
00:18:05,280 --> 00:18:07,740
was a long ugly scar
 running down his cheek.

507
00:18:07,740 --> 00:18:10,660
-Ah, Aphtali?

508
00:18:10,660 --> 00:18:11,980
-Who is he?

509
00:18:11,980 --> 00:18:13,890
-One of Mogol's soldiers.

510
00:18:13,890 --> 00:18:15,330
And the right arm of the queen.

511
00:18:15,330 --> 00:18:16,710
-The queen?

512
00:18:16,710 --> 00:18:18,560
-Is she against you?

513
00:18:18,560 --> 00:18:20,160
-Yes.

514
00:18:20,160 --> 00:18:21,070
I'm afraid so.

515
00:18:21,070 --> 00:18:22,780
[BUZZER] Uh-- Sarah, could
 you get us some coffee?

516
00:18:22,780 --> 00:18:24,770
-When her father, the
 late king was dying,

517
00:18:24,770 --> 00:18:26,760
the last thing he
 said to me was--

518
00:18:26,760 --> 00:18:27,770
[DEATH RATTLE]

519
00:18:27,770 --> 00:18:29,130
-Watch over Samara.

520
00:18:29,130 --> 00:18:30,820
Guide her-- Council her.

521
00:18:30,820 --> 00:18:34,200
At the time I thought my
 task would be an easy one.

522
00:18:34,200 --> 00:18:38,450
However, full of arrogance,
 and limitless pride.

523
00:18:38,450 --> 00:18:39,610
I hate that woman.

524
00:18:39,610 --> 00:18:42,460
But even with
 unrestrained ambition,

525
00:18:42,460 --> 00:18:44,630
I tried to induce her
 to rebel against the--

526
00:18:44,630 --> 00:18:45,160
-Oh, sure, but--

527
00:18:45,160 --> 00:18:47,250
-That for years
 has hung over us.

528
00:18:47,250 --> 00:18:48,070
-You lost me.

529
00:18:48,070 --> 00:18:50,190
-Everything third
 new moon, our youth

530
00:18:50,190 --> 00:18:54,400
is decimated by a sacrifice
 that's barbaric and inhuman.

531
00:18:54,400 --> 00:18:59,980
The next sacrifice
 takes place tomorrow.

532
00:18:59,980 --> 00:19:00,740
Hercules--

533
00:19:00,740 --> 00:19:01,770
-Let's have cookies outside.

