-I am always getting
 into these situations,

1582
00:56:09,440 --> 00:56:10,920
Call it Life of Riley.

1583
00:56:14,360 --> 00:56:16,830
-Hm?

1584
00:56:16,830 --> 00:56:18,120
[WARNING BUZZER]

1585
00:56:18,120 --> 00:56:21,590
-Plot point-- plot point--
 plot point-- plot point.

1586
00:56:21,590 --> 00:56:22,580
[WHISTLING]

1587
00:56:22,580 --> 00:56:23,800
-Come, Hercules.

1588
00:56:23,800 --> 00:56:25,610
Come and drink to
 our friendship.

1589
00:56:25,610 --> 00:56:27,270
-Hm, now you would
 assume that I would

1590
00:56:27,270 --> 00:56:29,120
think that the poison
 was in this cup.

1591
00:56:29,120 --> 00:56:31,980
-We'll toast our union-- the
 strongest force in the world.

1592
00:56:31,980 --> 00:56:33,230
-I want the Garfield cup.

1593
00:56:33,230 --> 00:56:35,510
-We don't know what the
 future has in store for us.

1594
00:56:35,510 --> 00:56:36,920
But you'll never be
 sorry that you've

1595
00:56:36,920 --> 00:56:40,930
taken your place at my side.

1596
00:56:40,930 --> 00:56:42,900
-Hm, his lips are strong too.

1597
00:56:45,780 --> 00:56:46,800
-My queen.

1598
00:56:46,800 --> 00:56:47,620
-Get out.

1599
00:56:47,620 --> 00:56:51,400
-I'm sorry, majesty
 but it's urgent.

1600
00:56:51,400 --> 00:56:52,080
-Wait outside.

1601
00:56:52,080 --> 00:56:54,950
[CRIES OF DISGUST]

1602
00:56:54,950 --> 00:56:57,240
-Aren't we gonna find
 her irresistible now?

1603
00:57:02,870 --> 00:57:05,380
-Ohh, Herc's been
 working with Uta Hagen.

1604
00:57:05,380 --> 00:57:06,040
I guess.

1605
00:57:06,040 --> 00:57:07,240
-Good, Herc.

1606
00:57:07,240 --> 00:57:08,860
Good.

1607
00:57:08,860 --> 00:57:10,420
-Hm, Herc very sleepy.

1608
00:57:10,420 --> 00:57:11,230
Must get shut-eye.

1609
00:57:14,330 --> 00:57:17,260
-I'm so sleepy I can
 barely keep awake.

1610
00:57:17,260 --> 00:57:19,360
-Hm, now I think I'll
 dress him up a bit.

1611
00:57:19,360 --> 00:57:21,570
Hm.

1612
00:57:21,570 --> 00:57:25,740
-Well, who's next on my list?

1613
00:57:25,740 --> 00:57:27,170
-Darix Is alive.

1614
00:57:27,170 --> 00:57:28,750
-And well and living in Vegas.

1615
00:57:28,750 --> 00:57:30,890
-He was rescued by Hercules
 who who fell upon us

1616
00:57:30,890 --> 00:57:32,830
and massacred the entire escort.

1617
00:57:32,830 --> 00:57:34,260
-Where's Darix now?

1618
00:57:34,260 --> 00:57:35,090
-I don't know, my queen.

1619
00:57:35,090 --> 00:57:35,920
I was badly wounded.

1620
00:57:35,920 --> 00:57:37,670
But I managed to
 drag myself here.

1621
00:57:37,670 --> 00:57:39,850
-To tell her you
 failed in your mission?

1622
00:57:39,850 --> 00:57:41,590
Execute him.

1623
00:57:41,590 --> 00:57:42,770
-No-- No-- No!

1624
00:57:42,770 --> 00:57:43,610
-Harsh.

1625
00:57:43,610 --> 00:57:45,520
-Darix free means
 trouble for us.

1626
00:57:45,520 --> 00:57:47,720
We must capture him.

1627
00:57:47,720 --> 00:57:49,460
-That's not difficult.

1628
00:57:49,460 --> 00:57:51,790
All we have to do
 is follow Agar.

1629
00:57:51,790 --> 00:57:52,980
-And follow our bliss.

1630
00:57:52,980 --> 00:57:53,480
-Hm.

1631
00:57:58,670 --> 00:58:02,160
[ACAPELLA SAXOPHONE]

1632
00:58:02,160 --> 00:58:04,230
-Oh yeah, it's a buffet.

1633
00:58:04,230 --> 00:58:07,490
-You thought you could trick
 Samara, but I'm too clever.

1634
00:58:07,490 --> 00:58:08,320
[SNORING]

1635
00:58:08,320 --> 00:58:11,620
-When at last you wake up you'll
 be my most faithful slave.

1636
00:58:16,060 --> 00:58:18,680
-You know, all these movies
 revolve around Herc sleeping.

1637
00:58:18,680 --> 00:58:19,180
-Mhm.

1638
00:58:19,180 --> 00:58:21,440
It's because he can
 remember how to do it.

1639
00:58:25,770 --> 00:58:28,020
-Why's he laying on a
 big cupcake wrapper?

1640
00:58:28,020 --> 00:58:28,660
-He's cream-filled.

1641
00:58:28,660 --> 00:58:30,760
-Ohh.

1642
00:58:30,760 --> 00:58:31,640
-Herc, you scamp.

1643
00:58:31,640 --> 00:58:33,290
-Doh-ho-ho.

1644
00:58:33,290 --> 00:58:35,410
-You know, I've
 been to paradise,

1645
00:58:35,410 --> 00:58:36,740
but I've never been to me.

1646
00:58:36,740 --> 00:58:38,870
Hm, nice-- nice digs.

1647
00:58:38,870 --> 00:58:42,250
-Fluff these up-- sit back.

1648
00:58:42,250 --> 00:58:45,050
Just wait for the
 chicks to roll in.

1649
00:58:45,050 --> 00:58:49,760
-Life of Riley--
 yup, Life of Riley.

1650
00:58:49,760 --> 00:58:51,190
It's good.

1651
00:58:51,190 --> 00:58:57,250
[THEME MUSIC]

1652
00:58:57,250 --> 00:58:59,520
-He's there to
 conspire against me.

1653
00:58:59,520 --> 00:59:01,060
You've helped our
 enemies and you've

1654
00:59:01,060 --> 00:59:02,030
fallen in love with Hercules.

1655
00:59:02,030 --> 00:59:03,090
-Good job, McLeod.

1656
00:59:03,090 --> 00:59:04,520
-I ought to punish you
 with death for this.

1657
00:59:04,520 --> 00:59:07,080
But too much blood
 has already been shed.

1658
00:59:07,080 --> 00:59:09,690
And now that Hercules
 is in my power,

1659
00:59:09,690 --> 00:59:11,850
you no longer represent
 any danger to us.

1660
00:59:11,850 --> 00:59:12,600
[GOBBLING]

1661
00:59:12,600 --> 00:59:13,960
-Get out.

1662
00:59:13,960 --> 00:59:16,580
I banish you from Samar.

1663
00:59:16,580 --> 00:59:18,400
Leave my kingdom forever.

1664
00:59:18,400 --> 00:59:19,200
-You're fired.

1665
00:59:19,200 --> 00:59:20,140
Clean out your dress.

1666
00:59:24,020 --> 00:59:28,970
[SOBBING]

1667
00:59:28,970 --> 00:59:30,350
-Now, way to banish her.

1668
00:59:30,350 --> 00:59:30,850
Huh.

1669
00:59:30,850 --> 00:59:33,140
You're great.

1670
00:59:33,140 --> 00:59:34,480
-(SINGING) It's the
 shiny little hiney

1671
00:59:34,480 --> 00:59:36,250
with the fringe on the top.

1672
00:59:36,250 --> 00:59:36,740
[CHUCKLING]

1673
00:59:36,740 --> 00:59:37,240
-I must dress.

1674
00:59:37,240 --> 00:59:38,680
-No, you mustn't.

1675
00:59:38,680 --> 00:59:39,660
Your wound hasn't healed.

1676
00:59:39,660 --> 00:59:40,880
And where would you go?

1677
00:59:40,880 --> 00:59:43,170
The minute you go outside
 they'll catch you.

1678
00:59:43,170 --> 00:59:45,290
-Timor, you've already
 taken great risks.

1679
00:59:45,290 --> 00:59:46,600
And I'm very grateful.

1680
00:59:46,600 --> 00:59:48,120
-Iron my pants, will you?

1681
00:59:48,120 --> 00:59:50,160
-But I cannot wait any longer.

1682
00:59:50,160 --> 00:59:51,400
-Oh, please, here
 put your top on.

1683
00:59:51,400 --> 00:59:52,460
You'll feel better.

1684
00:59:52,460 --> 00:59:55,360
-Billis has completely
 disappeared,

1685
00:59:55,360 --> 00:59:58,430
Hercules is in the dungeons
 and there's no news from Agar.

1686
00:59:58,430 --> 00:59:59,790
-There-- Doesn't
 that make it nice?

1687
00:59:59,790 --> 01:00:01,890
-Perhaps she's also in
 the hands of the queen.

1688
01:00:01,890 --> 01:00:04,280
-Well, who hasn't been in
 the hands of the queen.

1689
01:00:04,280 --> 01:00:06,050
-Soon it will be night and
 I must talk to our friend.

1690
01:00:06,050 --> 01:00:06,820
-Now cough.

1691
01:00:06,820 --> 01:00:07,590
-See how weak you are?

1692
01:00:07,590 --> 01:00:08,170
I'll go myself.

1693
01:00:08,170 --> 01:00:09,120
Just tell me what to say.

1694
01:00:09,120 --> 01:00:09,620
[KNOCKING]

1695
01:00:09,620 --> 01:00:10,950
-Timor, it's Agar.

1696
01:00:10,950 --> 01:00:11,940
Open up.

1697
01:00:11,940 --> 01:00:13,850
-Ah, lousy Jehovah's witnesses.

1698
01:00:13,850 --> 01:00:14,760
Hey, For wait a minute.

1699
01:00:14,760 --> 01:00:16,110
I'll get rid of them.

1700
01:00:16,110 --> 01:00:17,380
-Yeah.

1701
01:00:17,380 --> 01:00:18,310
-Uh-- Hi, look.

1702
01:00:18,310 --> 01:00:21,070
We just sat down
 to breakfast-- Oh.

1703
01:00:21,070 --> 01:00:21,570
-Agar.

1704
01:00:21,570 --> 01:00:22,360
We thought you were--

1705
01:00:22,360 --> 01:00:22,860
-Yes.

1706
01:00:22,860 --> 01:00:24,310
But I was sent into exile.

1707
01:00:24,310 --> 01:00:26,010
We must try to save Hercules.

1708
01:00:26,010 --> 01:00:26,880
-And Billis?

1709
01:00:26,880 --> 01:00:28,450
-She wasn't among
 the other victims.

1710
01:00:28,450 --> 01:00:29,510
-Where is she?

1711
01:00:29,510 --> 01:00:30,280
-I don't know.

1712
01:00:30,280 --> 01:00:35,480
Hercules was trying
 to find her. [SCREAM]

1713
01:00:35,480 --> 01:00:35,980
-Don't run.

1714
01:00:35,980 --> 01:00:36,480
LAPD.

1715
01:00:40,250 --> 01:00:46,590
[ACAPELLA DRUMMING]

1716
01:00:46,590 --> 01:00:47,610
-Ooh.

1717
01:00:47,610 --> 01:00:48,780
Is this 926 Maple?

1718
01:00:48,780 --> 01:00:49,440
Aw, geez.

1719
01:00:49,440 --> 01:00:50,270
We got the wrong address.

1720
01:00:50,270 --> 01:00:52,560
Sorry.

1721
01:00:52,560 --> 01:00:56,230
-Meanwhile, in Heff's grotto.

1722
01:00:56,230 --> 01:00:57,620
-(SINGING) Come
 here, young children

1723
01:00:57,620 --> 01:01:00,050
and bring me your wine.

1724
01:01:00,050 --> 01:01:02,950
Ohhh, bitter dregs.

1725
01:01:02,950 --> 01:01:03,690
-Send them away.

1726
01:01:07,470 --> 01:01:09,090
-Now to bring them back.

1727
01:01:09,090 --> 01:01:10,860
I love it when you do that.

1728
01:01:10,860 --> 01:01:11,360
-Fine.

1729
01:01:11,360 --> 01:01:13,730
-Is that a polar bear rug?

1730
01:01:13,730 --> 01:01:14,320
Oh, no.

1731
01:01:14,320 --> 01:01:14,910
It's his horse.

1732
01:01:14,910 --> 01:01:17,600
-Why did you ride
 here to do that?

1733
01:01:17,600 --> 01:01:19,680
-Because I wanted to
 be alone with you.

1734
01:01:19,680 --> 01:01:24,290
-Because I want to know what
 makes you, Queen Samara, tick.

1735
01:01:24,290 --> 01:01:27,760
[KISSING] Hey, you
 taste like Steve Reeves.

1736
01:01:27,760 --> 01:01:28,260
Yeah.

1737
01:01:28,260 --> 01:01:30,150
Mhm.

1738
01:01:30,150 --> 01:01:31,070
-Samara.

1739
01:01:31,070 --> 01:01:33,640
You told me many
 marvelous things.

1740
01:01:33,640 --> 01:01:36,570
-You told me a fabricated story
 that wouldn't convince a child.

1741
01:01:36,570 --> 01:01:41,290
-You said that at
 your side I would

1742
01:01:41,290 --> 01:01:43,740
become the most powerful
 man in the world.

1743
01:01:43,740 --> 01:01:46,950
Yet, you never explained
 how these things

1744
01:01:46,950 --> 01:01:47,580
would come to pass.

1745
01:01:47,580 --> 01:01:48,080
-Hey, Herc.

1746
01:01:48,080 --> 01:01:50,180
James Brolin wants
 his beard back.

1747
01:01:50,180 --> 01:01:52,800
-After tonight, you'll
 know the answer.

1748
01:01:52,800 --> 01:01:55,360
-I don't understand how in
 the space of a few hours

1749
01:01:55,360 --> 01:01:57,190
you can change our destiny.

1750
01:01:57,190 --> 01:01:59,600
What can happen of
 such great importance?

1751
01:01:59,600 --> 01:02:02,300
-You must have faith in me.

1752
01:02:02,300 --> 01:02:05,010
Tonight you'll be at my
 side and you'll know.

1753
01:02:05,010 --> 01:02:06,620
You'll be able to see
 with your own eyes

1754
01:02:06,620 --> 01:02:07,870
that I've told you the truth.

1755
01:02:07,870 --> 01:02:08,840
-I saw it with my own eyes.

1756
01:02:08,840 --> 01:02:10,140
What a dumb expression.

1757
01:02:10,140 --> 01:02:13,150
-The important thing now is
 that you tell me you love me.

1758
01:02:13,150 --> 01:02:14,660
-On our first date?

1759
01:02:14,660 --> 01:02:15,900
Ouch.

1760
01:02:15,900 --> 01:02:17,890
-I love you, Samara.

1761
01:02:17,890 --> 01:02:19,650
-And you've never loved
 anyone else as much?

1762
01:02:19,650 --> 01:02:21,610
-Well, I had a dog once, but--

1763
01:02:24,390 --> 01:02:25,640
-Do you think I wear
 too much makeup?

1764
01:02:29,390 --> 01:02:34,640
[SLURPING]

1765
01:02:34,640 --> 01:02:38,120
-Oh, JP Morgan gonged her.

1766
01:02:38,120 --> 01:02:38,620
-Ooh.

1767
01:02:42,520 --> 01:02:43,100
-My blankie.

1768
01:02:46,340 --> 01:02:48,110
-You know them?

1769
01:02:48,110 --> 01:02:49,890
-Yes.

1770
01:02:49,890 --> 01:02:52,540
-They were the ones who
 tried to set me against you.

1771
01:02:52,540 --> 01:02:53,040
-And she?

1772
01:02:53,040 --> 01:02:54,860
Wasn't she your friend?

1773
01:02:54,860 --> 01:02:55,740
-Friend?

1774
01:02:55,740 --> 01:02:58,300
She's just a girl who took
 me in, like the others.

1775
01:02:58,300 --> 01:02:59,370
-How can you betray us?

1776
01:02:59,370 --> 01:03:01,160
-I told you that you were
 completely in my power,

1777
01:03:01,160 --> 01:03:02,660
didn't I?

1778
01:03:02,660 --> 01:03:05,230
And I also ordered you
 to get out of my kingdom.

1779
01:03:05,230 --> 01:03:07,250
-And Isaac Hayes
 wants his vest back.

1780
01:03:07,250 --> 01:03:09,330
-What sentence shall
 I decree for them.

1781
01:03:09,330 --> 01:03:10,070
-Hmm.

1782
01:03:10,070 --> 01:03:13,140
Something crunchy.

1783
01:03:13,140 --> 01:03:14,260
-The death penalty.

1784
01:03:14,260 --> 01:03:14,840
-All around.

1785
01:03:14,840 --> 01:03:15,520
On the house.

1786
01:03:15,520 --> 01:03:18,130
-A slow death.

1787
01:03:18,130 --> 01:03:19,530
Let them die of starvation.

1788
01:03:19,530 --> 01:03:22,320
Give them plenty
 of time to regret

1789
01:03:22,320 --> 01:03:24,420
having taken up
 arms against you.

1790
01:03:24,420 --> 01:03:25,920
-This isn't you.

1791
01:03:25,920 --> 01:03:27,220
It's not possible.

1792
01:03:27,220 --> 01:03:28,590
-He's right.

1793
01:03:28,590 --> 01:03:29,820
Take them away.

1794
01:03:29,820 --> 01:03:31,390
And see that the
 orders are carried out.

1795
01:03:31,390 --> 01:03:31,890
-Right.

1796
01:03:31,890 --> 01:03:33,320
Two slow deaths coming up.

1797
01:03:33,320 --> 01:03:35,770
-Hey, Bob, We need
 two slow deaths.

1798
01:03:35,770 --> 01:03:37,250
Rack them.

1799
01:03:37,250 --> 01:03:38,240
-Snaggletoothy.

1800
01:03:38,240 --> 01:03:40,240
-Listen to me.

1801
01:03:40,240 --> 01:03:43,200
I understand your doubts
 because I share them.

1802
01:03:43,200 --> 01:03:45,340
Did you think I was
 naturally a war-like spirit?

1803
01:03:45,340 --> 01:03:46,090
-Well, yes.

1804
01:03:46,090 --> 01:03:47,900
-I am only a tavern-keeper.

1805
01:03:47,900 --> 01:03:50,170
But also I know that this is
 the moment for us to stand up

1806
01:03:50,170 --> 01:03:51,410
like men or we'll
 never know what

1807
01:03:51,410 --> 01:03:52,600
it is to be free men again.

1808
01:03:52,600 --> 01:03:53,100
[GROANING]

1809
01:03:53,100 --> 01:03:54,370
-And just what do
 you expect us to do?

1810
01:03:54,370 --> 01:03:55,610
They know who we
 are and soon they'll

1811
01:03:55,610 --> 01:03:57,530
be coming here to arrest us.

1812
01:03:57,530 --> 01:03:58,480
-Timor's been killed.

1813
01:03:58,480 --> 01:04:00,030
Darix is in the
 hands of the queen

1814
01:04:00,030 --> 01:04:02,140
and we don't even know
 whether Hercules is alive.

1815
01:04:02,140 --> 01:04:03,900
-Hercules isn't a
 man to let himself

1816
01:04:03,900 --> 01:04:05,030
be put out of the
 way that easily.

1817
01:04:05,030 --> 01:04:06,490
-I agree with Thersius.

1818
01:04:06,490 --> 01:04:07,630
I have a son.

1819
01:04:07,630 --> 01:04:09,560
I don't know whether
 he's dead or alive.

1820
01:04:09,560 --> 01:04:10,970
But that doesn't
 change anything.

1821
01:04:10,970 --> 01:04:11,650
-Let me in, I say.

1822
01:04:11,650 --> 01:04:12,810
-Orders are orders.

1823
01:04:12,810 --> 01:04:13,620
-Soldiers.

1824
01:04:13,620 --> 01:04:14,580
-You can let him in, Reinon.

1825
01:04:14,580 --> 01:04:15,870
-Chong.

1826
01:04:15,870 --> 01:04:17,470
-An officer of the royal guards.

1827
01:04:17,470 --> 01:04:18,850
-Can we get some service here?

1828
01:04:18,850 --> 01:04:19,350
-Rubio.

1829
01:04:19,350 --> 01:04:20,150
What are you doing here?

1830
01:04:20,150 --> 01:04:22,320
-I know just what you and your
 companions are plotting to do

1831
01:04:22,320 --> 01:04:24,220
and it would have been very
 easy for me to have taken you

1832
01:04:24,220 --> 01:04:25,930
by surprise and had
 you put to death.

1833
01:04:25,930 --> 01:04:26,740
-It's John DeLorean!

1834
01:04:26,740 --> 01:04:28,250
-Instead I'm asking
 to let me join you.

1835
01:04:28,250 --> 01:04:29,690
The Army is with me.

1836
01:04:29,690 --> 01:04:32,140
We must fight together against
 Mogol and the household guard.

1837
01:04:32,140 --> 01:04:34,130
-Are you serious?

1838
01:04:34,130 --> 01:04:36,410
You who have sworn
 a military oath?

1839
01:04:36,410 --> 01:04:38,250
-No man of honor can
 be tied by an oath that

1840
01:04:38,250 --> 01:04:40,590
requires that he cover
